hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19285","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Thawr, he said: Rashid ibn Sad narrated to me from Abdullah ibn Luhayy from Abdullah ibn Qurt that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The greatest days with Allah are the Day of Sacrifice then the Day of Nafr. Five or six camels were brought to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to slaughter them. They crowded toward him, which of them he begins with. When their sides fell he said a hidden word I did not understand. I asked one near me: What did he say? They said: He said: Whoever wishes let him cut off."
"19286","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us from Bakr ibn Zurah al-Khawlani from Muslim ibn Abdullah al-Azdi who said: Abdullah ibn Qurt al-Azdi came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Are you Abdullah ibn Qurt?"
